---
term: Charter graph
aka:
  - Network of charters
section: structure
order: 60
definition: The web of relationships among all charters in the Social Charter.
example: A farm cooperative delegates its economic authority to an agricultural federation and its territorial authority to a county corporation. It answers to each parent only within that parent's domain.
seeAlso:
  - nested-corporation
  - representation-vector
---
The system is a graph, not a simple tree. A corporation can have several parents, each covering a different dimension of its interests, so it can take part in several institutional dimensions at once.
